every year Netflix ups the game with its  original content in fact the streaming  service will soon boast 1,000 original  movies and shows in its library you'll  probably never be able to watch them all  but there's no denying that there's  truly something for everyone available  the company is already hard at work  putting out tantalizing glimpses of  their 2019 lineup from a gangster film  by Martin Scorsese to a brand-new  superhero series 2019 is shaping up to  be an epic year here's a look at  everything we know about the 2019  Netflix originals that are sure to blow  you away  the Irishman barely five years ago it  would have been insane to suggest that  Martin Scorsese would direct a direct to  streaming feature but now that video  on-demand services are backing  oscar-winning films like Amazon's  Manchester by the sea it's safe to say  that the landscape has changed and with  Netflix willing to dump billions in the  pot for new original content who can  blame Scorsese for working out a  production deal the result sees the  Goodfellas director going back to his  roots with the Irishman a mob epic  starring Robert De Niro as Frank Sheeran  the Hitman allegedly responsible for the  disappearance of Jimmy Hoffa De Niro  isn't the only big name attached  Al Pacino is on board to play Hoffa with  Joe Pesci Harvey Keitel and Anna Paquin  co-starring  the Central Park five with the  hard-hitting documentary xiii ava  duvernay proved beyond a shadow of a  doubt that she could handle sensitive  real-life struggles in a way that  resonated with Netflix's audience so it  should come as no surprise that the  streaming service is tapping her for an  in-depth dive into one of the most  infamous crimes of the 80s in 1989 New  Yorker Tricia Miley was jogging in  Central Park when she was assaulted  police subsequently arrested five  teenagers who were convicted and  sentenced to prison  it wasn't until over a decade later that  the real perpetrator confessed proving  the five young men to be innocent the  Central Park five will be a scripted  drama series that explores the aftermath  of the crime from the media circus  surrounding the trials to the young  men's eventual release from prison  it should offer an emotional look into  how the case affected the lives of  everyone involved sex education one of  the bright spots of 2019 should be  Gillian Anderson's return to the small  screen after leaving both the x-files  and American Gods she slated to star in  sex education as Jean a therapist and  working mom who's trying her best to  raise her son Otis who's a bit of an odd  duck he's a virgin who knows more about  getting busy than any of his sheets  shaking classmates asa butterfield who  you may know from Ender's Game stars as  Otis and the series is slated for a  tentative 2019 release date the last  dance in the 90s there was only one name  that mattered in basketball Michael  Jordan as the scoreboard stacking star  of the Chicago Bulls Jordan became both  an athletic legend and a pop culture  icon he brought whole stadiums to their  feet with his buzzer beaters and rim  rattling dunks with the last dance  Netflix is teaming up with ESPN to  deliver a one-of-a-kind look at the  sports climate of the early 90s when air  jordan soared to stardom the ten part  documentary series will combine  interviews with jordan and his former  teammates along with archival footage of  the Bulls final bid for one more  championship in 1998 put it all together  and it should be a unique enthralling  experience for any sports fan polar from  Bond villain to cannibal genius Maz  Mickelson has practically done it all  which is why it's almost surprising that  he's found yet another exceptionally  unique project to tackle Netflix's  upcoming polar is based on polar came  from the cold a graphic novel that  follows a retired assassin who's forced  back into his old ways after an attempt  on his life the concept began life as a  webcomic before Dark Horse picked it up  and turned it into a graphic novel and  it's about as crazy as you'd expect from  its hyper violence to its Bleak neo-noir  trappings Poehler came from the cold is  certainly an experience and we're hoping  the film finds a way to capture that  insanity pickle sin is taking the lead  role with Vanessa Hudgens and Katheryn  Winnick  signed on to CoStar razing Dion in 2015  writer and director Dennis Liu wrote and  released a comic book series called  raising Dion accompanied by a trailer to  promote it the comic follows a single  mother who realizes that her  seven-year-old son Dion is developing  superpowers it's a unique completely  different type of superhero story than  many people are used to and the first  issue snagged plenty of fans it didn't  take long for Netflix to take notice  ordering a ten episode series with Blu  at the helm this series will follow the  same story as the comic with Alicia  Wainwright starring as Dion's mother and  Michael B Jordan as her husband in a  climate filled with superheroes of all  shapes and forms  Raising Dion definitely looks like an  original take on the genre Dolomites is  my name Eddie Murphy has flown way under  the radar for the past two several years  so it's big news that he's set to appear  in a new project in Dolomites is my name  he stars as Rudy ray Moore a comedian  and actor best known for starring in the  1975 exploitation film Dolomites Moore  had a long varied career in both  stand-up and the film industry so there  really isn't a better actor to bring him  to life the supporting cast is just a  star studded with Wesley Snipes TI &amp;  keegan-michael key all set to appear  even Chris Rock was spotted on set  decked out in the kind of outfit that  could have only come from the 70s
 

